==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 60~120 seconds<sup>1,800f~3,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
**20 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
**10 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
**20 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
**30 [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring ranged [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] that can quickly kill a large group of the Zoges and damage the base quickly as well. The level itself is very straightforward with only two different enemies besides [[Ms. Sign]], so as long as you can consistently stall your frontline with attackers, the level can be cleared with ease.

==Trivia==
*Home Sweet Mausoleum's Japanese name, Shiryō no Yakata (死霊の館, "Estate of Spirits") is a reference to ''Shiryō-kan'' (死霊館, "Spirit Estate"), the Japanese name of [[wikipedia:The Conjuring|''The Conjuring'']].
*Home Sweet Mausoleum is the first [[Stories of Legend]] stage to contain [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies.

